  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-31 by an independent auditor who authored none of the change. RFC text (rfc8654): \"Similarly, any speaker that treats an improper BGP Extended Message as a fatal error MUST follow the error-handling procedures of [RFC4271].\" Producers moved: relay_recovery.go departedOwner now tests adjOutOwnerSessionCurrent rather than adjOutOwnerCurrent (30ff1fce91/fa6552968f), so a departure stays a session fact and a live session's policy-stale path is not counted departed; the routes of the closed session are still the ones owed withdrawal or replacement, which is what RFC 4271 Section 6 requires. session_read.go readAndProcessMessage and session_coalesce.go readAndProcessCoalesced (ff2aac12b0) gained a beginAdmission gate that holds a fully read packet while a policy change pauses admission; in readAndProcessMessage it sits after hdr.ValidateLengthWithMax, so an over-length message still returns its error and takes the NOTIFICATION path before the gate. All seven tagged units are byte-identical. Verdict unchanged: enforced. Earlier judgements are in this file's git history.",
